<Base title="Your numbers stay with you." description="How Howloop handles calculator inputs, saved plans, email, hosting, fonts and advertising."><header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / privacy</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">HOWLOOP · THE DETAILS</span><h1 style="max-width:900px">Your numbers stay with you.</h1></header><article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 18 September 2026</p><p>This policy applies to howloop.how. It describes the current calculator implementation and the advertising features that may be enabled later.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Calculations run in your browser. The website does not send the amounts you enter to Howloop or to a bank. We do not ask for bank logins or connect to financial accounts. The bank picker downloads public product snapshots hosted on this site.</p><h2>Saving on your device</h2><p>Choosing “Save on this device” writes your calculator inputs and selected product to local storage in that browser. They remain there until you choose “Clear saved plan” or clear site data. Anyone with access to that browser profile may be able to view saved inputs. A downloaded CSV is a file on your device; manage or delete it using your device’s file controls.</p><h2>Site requests and email</h2><p>The hosting provider processes ordinary connection information such as IP address, request time, browser details and the page requested to deliver and protect the site. If you email us, your email provider and ours process the message and we receive what you choose to send. Avoid sending sensitive financial or identity information. Contact us to ask about correspondence you have sent.</p><h2>Fonts and external links</h2><p>We load the DM Sans typeface from Google Fonts. The request may disclose your IP address and technical request information to Google. Links to banks, government resources and other websites take you to services with their own privacy policies.</p><h2>Cookies and advertising</h2><p>The current calculator release does not load advertising scripts or analytics tracking. Saved plans use local storage only when you choose to save. We may introduce Google AdSense after completing account and site setup.</p><p>If Google ads are enabled, Google and other advertising vendors may use cookies to serve ads based on visits to this and other websites. Google’s advertising cookies can support personalised ads. You can manage personalisation at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google Ads Settings</a> and find third-party choices at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">YourAdChoices</a>. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>.</p><p>Before advertising is enabled, this policy and the site’s consent controls must reflect the actual setup. Applicable regional consent requirements, including Google’s certified consent-platform requirements for relevant European traffic, need to be configured by the site operator.</p><h2>Contact and changes</h2><p>For privacy questions or requests about correspondence, email <a href="mailto:hello@howloop.how">hello@howloop.how</a>. Browser-stored calculator inputs can be removed directly on your device. This policy will be updated when the site’s data practices change.</p></article></Base>
